<title>MALAYSIA: Malaysia Konsortium unit buys ships.</title>
<headline>Malaysia Konsortium unit buys ships.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Konsortium Perkapalan Bhd said on Friday that its unit PNSL Bhd has placed orders valued at 134 million ringgit for two 73,000 dead weight tonnes (DWT) bulk carriers from Hyundai Heavy Industries of Korea.</p>
<p>In a statement, Konsortium said the bulk carriers, which have been upgraded from the standard shipyard specification, will be ready in 1999.</p>
<p>PNSL's fleet comprises 58 vessels with a combined capacity of 1.58 million dwt.</p>
<p>Konsortium also said that it has secured approval from the Malaysian Securities Commission (SC) for the consolidation of its shipping interests into Diperdana Corp Bhd.</p>
<p>In the previously announced deal with Diperdana, Konsortium is transferring its shipping assets to Diperdana, and taking on haulage businesses.</p>
<p>Konsortium said it intends to change the name of its shipping arm to PNSL Holdings Bhd.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603 201 4813)</p>
